# Installed Editor Save evidence verifier

This metadata-only campaign authenticates the installed repository-root verifier against the unchanged Editor Save public evidence. Syntax, default historical verification, and `--require-current` verification passed. Both verification calls authenticated 174 distinct evidence byte objects, 516 epoch path records, 21 frozen plan artifacts, eight installed product files, and the source-bound current 78/78 receipt. All 31 live Editor/shared source hashes match that receipt.

The earlier verifier was mistakenly created at `products/rea-studio/scripts/verify-editor-save-followup.mjs`. Its exact 6,767 bytes and SHA-256 `00c25f3c8dade731d5a60595126bd49a93fec8b9ce395a9c3f529c5896f1634f` are preserved here and already in the unchanged 43-file current test evidence. The owned misplaced live file was removed after authenticating its snapshot. The requested `scripts/verify-editor-save-followup.mjs` uses a single explicit repository-root declaration adjustment, recorded in `source-transform.json`; all assertions and evidence paths are otherwise byte-identical. This later tool-location change does not rebind the prior behavioral run or its source set. The initial misplaced script was added after the behavioral collection and had no test-file suffix. Its filesystem timestamps are retained, and the parent owns interpretation of the concurrently running global source census.

The parent reported a `MODULE_NOT_FOUND` attempt before the requested script was installed. This is an installation-order/location diagnostic, with no app execution. Its original raw output remains with the parent; this folder does not invent or claim that raw transcript. No new application behavior tests, original Editor engine executions, browser actions, or benchmarks were run in this campaign.

The frozen 21-file plan's prose says 16 selected test files. Its actual selector and census contain 15 files and 78 registrations; the 78-test total is correct. This finite metadata correction is explicit here and in the prior current receipt. Old plan, stage, review, failed-run, and current43 evidence remain unchanged. This verifier supports finite evidence accounting, not full Editor compatibility or performance claims.

`validation.json` binds all three invocation results and raw streams, the exact installed script, and before/after frozen evidence anchors. `freeze-manifest.json` inventories every file in this folder except itself. The verifier writes no files and runs no app tests.
